---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Card from '../components/card.astro';
import Quill from '../components/Quill.astro';
import EnomeND from '../components/enomeND.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <main class="content-wrap">
    <div class="one-column">
      <h1 class="page-title">Developing apps for a brighter tomorrow.</h1>
      <EnomeND />
      <Quill />
      <section class="card-row">
        <Card title="Live Project: Christian Therapy Practice">
          <p>
            A fully deployed website built for a Christian therapist, designed to communicate a
            Christ-centered understanding of care with clarity, professionalism, and warmth.
          </p>
          <p>
            This project reflects how faith, ethics, and thoughtful design can work together in a
            real-world clinical practice.
          </p>

          <p>
            <a href="https://thelionslamb.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              View the live site →
            </a>
          </p>
        </Card>

        <Card title="In Development: Financial Clarity Tools">
          <p>
            I am developing analytical tools designed to bring clarity to personal and system-level
            financial decisions, bringing income, expenses, obligations, and debt into a single,
            understandable view.
          </p>
          <p>
            This work focuses on reducing noise in complex financial systems, including both
            traditional finance and emerging digital assets.
          </p>
          <p><em>Currently in active development.</em></p>
        </Card>

        <Card title="Exploring: Reading Comprehension Builder">
          <p>
            I am designing a tool that helps students understand what they read by slowing the
            process down in the right way. Students read a short section, click <strong>Next</strong>,
            and answer a few questions before moving on.
          </p>
          <p>
            They can move back to reread anytime, but as they progress, questions become cumulative,
            requiring them to remember and connect details across multiple sections.
          </p>
          <p><em>Want to pilot this with students? <strong>Reach out.</strong></em></p>
        </Card>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    .content-wrap {
      max-width: 1200px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    }

    .one-column {
      display: block;
    }

    .page-title {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.75rem);
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
      color: antiquewhite;
    }

    .card-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
